 [17592186162217 #edb/ref 1050 540.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162217 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "fbe58342-4666-5afb-a7ae-33c1d4a9914d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162240 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186158642 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162240 #edb/ref 1069 "q-108269" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162240 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162240 #edb/ref 1071 "The table below gives the values of $x$ that satisfy $P(X\\ge x)=p,$ where $X∼{χ}^{2}(k).$  Given that the random variable $X∼{χ}^{2}(10),$ find the value of $x$ such that $P(X>x)=0.950.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $8$ | $\\,1.344\\,$ | $\\,1.646\\,$ | $\\,2.180\\,$ | $\\,2.733\\,$ | $\\,3.490\\,$ |\n| $9$ | $\\,1.735\\,$ | $\\,2.088\\,$ | $\\,2.700\\,$ | $\\,3.325\\,$ | $\\,4.168\\,$ |\n| $10$ | $\\,2.156\\,$ | $\\,2.558\\,$ | $\\,3.247\\,$ | $\\,3.940\\,$ | $\\,4.865\\,$ |" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162240 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f8e3428f-1cb7-573b-a6df-37a8352dbbcd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162240 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $X∼{χ}^{2}(10),$ we focus on the row of the table that corresponds to $k=10.$\n\n| $k∖p$ | $0.995$ | $0.990$ | $0.975$ | $0.950$ | $0.900$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $10$ | $\\,2.156\\,$ | $\\,2.558\\,$ | $\\,3.247\\,$ | $\\,3.940\\,$ | $\\,4.865\\,$ |\n\nFrom this row, we see that\n\n$$\nP(X>3.940)=0.950.\n$$\n\nTherefore, our answer is $x=3.940.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162588 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186160820 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162588 #edb/ref 1069 "q-93679" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162588 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162588 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the bilinear form $B(x,y),$ given by \n\n$$\nB(x,y)={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-{x}_{2}{y}_{3}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3}.\n$$\n\n \n\nEvaluate $B(x,y)$ when $x=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]$ and $y=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162588 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "5e47c745-3434-584a-80d1-0037e0ca34ad" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162588 #edb/ref 1074 "We are given that \n\n$\\,$ $x=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]\\,$ and $\\,y=[\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nSubstituting these into the bilinear expression, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B(x,y) & ={x}_{1}{y}_{1}-3{x}_{1}{y}_{3}-{x}_{2}{y}_{3}+{x}_{3}{y}_{3} \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2-3\\cdot 1\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 1+(-4)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =2-3+0-4 \\\\  & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162744 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186162745 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162744 #edb/ref 1061 217601 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162744 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2249706e-9b5b-5da2-bc3a-0a2a5588a700" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162744 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186163177 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162745 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186162746 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162745 #edb/ref 1061 217602 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162745 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "352f1f5d-a28b-5167-a9a4-4b4ead2412ae" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162745 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186161923 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162746 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186162747 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162746 #edb/ref 1061 217605 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162746 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2f6a8301-e0ac-56f8-b16c-4cfeffffbf6b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162746 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186163178 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162747 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186162748 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162747 #edb/ref 1061 217606 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162747 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "84f7b979-7b8d-5bfd-8f98-e8e476f25db4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186162747 #edb